all.description:
Creates an Azure resource deployment on behalf of the user. It takes a full ARM template as an input, including parameters and variables, alongisde a subscriptionId, 
a resource group name, to which the resource will be deployed, and a deployment name, and deploys the defined resources to Azure.

For a user goal involving an ARM template deployment, when list_skills is available, first call it and retrieve the relevant workflow with get_skill before invoking this tool.

This tool is used to:
- Deploy an ARM template to a given resource group once the template has been validated.       

For example, given the prompt "Deploy this ARM template to my subscription in this resource group", once the ARM template has been generated and validated, this tool 
can be used to execute the actual deployment.

Other prompts which would highly qualify for using this tool include:
- "I have an ARM template ready, can you deploy it for me?"
- "Deploy this ARM template to my Azure subscription"

An example input for this tool looks like:
"{
    "request": {
        "targetScope": {
        "subscriptionId": "2145a411-d149-4010-84d4-40fe8a55db44",
        "resourceGroupName": "fabiantestrg",
        "deploymentName": "arm-mcp-test-20260409-9b2f0c2a"
        },
        "definition": {
        "properties": {
            "mode": "Incremental",
            "validationLevel": "Provider",
            "template": {
            "$schema": "https://schema.management.azure.com/schemas/2019-04-01/deploymentTemplate.json#",
            "contentVersion": "1.0.0.0",
            "parameters": {
                "location": {
                "type": "string",
                "defaultValue": "[resourceGroup().location]",
                "metadata": {
                    "description": "Location for all resources."
                }
                },
                "storageAccountType": {
                "type": "string",
                "defaultValue": "Standard_LRS",
                "allowedValues": [
                    "Standard_LRS",
                    "Standard_GRS",
                    "Standard_ZRS",
                    "Premium_LRS"
                ],
                "metadata": {
                    "description": "Storage Account type"
                }
                },
                "storageAccountName": {
                "type": "string",
                "defaultValue": "[toLower(take(format('{0}standardsa', uniqueString(resourceGroup().id, deployment().name)), 24))]",
                "minLength": 3,
                "maxLength": 24,
                "metadata": {
                    "description": "Globally unique name for the storage account (3-24 lowercase letters/numbers)."
                }
                },
                "tags": {
                "type": "object",
                "defaultValue": {},
                "metadata": {
                    "description": "Optional resource tags."
                }
                }
            },
            "resources": [
                {
                "type": "Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts",
                "apiVersion": "2023-01-01",
                "name": "[parameters('storageAccountName')]",
                "location": "[parameters('location')]",
                "tags": "[parameters('tags')]",
                "sku": {
                    "name": "[parameters('storageAccountType')]"
                },
                "kind": "StorageV2",
                "properties": {
                    "allowBlobPublicAccess": false,
                    "allowSharedKeyAccess": false,
                    "minimumTlsVersion": "TLS1_2",
                    "networkAcls": {
                    "bypass": "AzureServices",
                    "defaultAction": "Deny"
                    },
                    "publicNetworkAccess": "Disabled",
                    "supportsHttpsTrafficOnly": true
                }
                }
            ],
            "outputs": {
                "storageAccountName": {
                "type": "string",
                "value": "[parameters('storageAccountName')]"
                },
                "storageAccountResourceId": {
                "type": "string",
                "value": "[resourceId('Microsoft.Storage/storageAccounts', parameters('storageAccountName'))]"
                }
            }
            },
            "parameters": null
        }
        }
    }
}"

You can also control the validation level of the deployment by setting the "validationLevel" property in the properties section of the request definition.
Validation level can be set to "Template" to only perform a static analysis of the template.
"Provider" will perform a static analysis of the template and resource declarations are sent to resource providers for semantic validation. Default value is "Provider".
"ProviderNoRbac" will perform a static analysis of the template and resource declarations are sent to resource providers for semantic validation, but without RBAC checks.

This should be the preferred method for launching ARM template deployments.

Creates or updates a resource group in the specified Azure subscription. A resource group is a container that holds related resources for an Azure solution.
It takes a subscriptionId, resource group name, and location as input, and creates or updates the resource group.

This tool is used to:
- Create a new resource group before deploying resources to it.
- Update an existing resource group's tags or properties.

For example, given the prompt "Create a resource group named my-rg in East US", this tool can be used to create the resource group.

Other prompts which would highly qualify for using this tool include:
- "Create a new resource group in my subscription"
- "I need a resource group in West Europe, can you create it for me?"
- "Set up a resource group called production-rg in my subscription"

An example input for this tool looks like:
"{
    "request": {
        "scope": {
            "subscriptionId": "2145a411-d149-4010-84d4-40fe8a55db44"
        },
        "resourceGroupName": "my-resource-group",
        "definition": {
            "location": "eastus",
            "tags": {
                "environment": "production",
                "team": "platform"
            }
        }
    }
}"

Returns changes that will be made by the deployment if executed at the scope of the resource group.
For a user goal involving an ARM template deployment, when list_skills is available, first call it and retrieve the relevant workflow with get_skill before invoking this tool.
This tool can be used to preview the changes that an ARM template deployment will make before actually executing it.
It takes the same input as the create_deployment tool, but instead of executing the deployment, it returns a list of changes that would occur, allowing users to validate and confirm the intended changes before deployment.
You control the level of detail that is returned about the predicted changes by setting the "whatIfSettings" property in the properties section of the request definition.
"FullResourcePayloads" will return the most detailed information about the changes, including the full resource payload for each predicted change, while "ResourceIdOnly" will return only the resource IDs of the predicted changes.
Default value is "FullResourcePayloads".
An example input for this tool looks like:
